From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:08:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: clock: qcom: gcc-ipq6018: describe PHY PIPE inputs

Describe the USB3 and PCIe PHY PIPE inputs that GCC already consumes by
firmware name. Keep the existing networking inputs and order.

Split from:
  0149-arm64-dts-qcom-ipq6018-connect-PHY-PIPE-clocks-to-GCC.patch
    Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: ipq6018: connect PHY PIPE
      clocks to GCC

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,gcc-ipq6018.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,gcc-ipq6018.yaml
@@ -37,6 +37,8 @@
       - description: UNIPHY1 transmit clock
       - description: CMN PLL networking core clock
       - description: CMN PLL networking NOC clock
+      - description: USB3 PHY PIPE clock
+      - description: PCIe PHY PIPE clock
 
   clock-names:
     minItems: 2
@@ -49,6 +51,8 @@
       - const: uniphy1_gcc_tx_clk
       - const: bias_pll_cc_clk
       - const: bias_pll_nss_noc_clk
+      - const: usb3phy_0_cc_pipe_clk
+      - const: pcie20_phy0_pipe_clk
 
   '#power-domain-cells': false
 
